"""Loop 9 (theme D): encoding and use -- retrieval, AI grounding, projections, annotation, usage and outcome feedback.

The articles say encoded process knowledge must be queryable, reasonable over and spread
consistently to the systems and AI agents that consume it; that what an AI is handed must be
governed, reasoned, provenanced and current; that diagrams and prose are generated from the model;
that discussion stays apart from it; and that usage and outcomes feed back into how knowledge is
managed. This model does not run an AI. It records what AI systems were given and what they
did -- retrievals, answers, prompts, tool calls, benchmarks -- as data, and every predicate here
judges those records against the shared model.
"""
